  "body": "**What happens:** the status line at the bottom of the main window shows its messages in dark grey on the near-black bar, so they're close to invisible. Refusals that explain why an action did nothing go unread. Two seen in one session (macOS, default dark theme):\n- \"operation not created: invalid parameters: no stock; set up stock first\"\n- \"operation not created: invalid parameters: a 2D Contour operation must cut downward: …\"\n\nTo the user, clicking **Face** or **2D Contour** just did nothing.\n\n**Expected:** status text meets the same readability gate as the rest of the theme (the WCAG contrast check the theme tokens already pass), and refusals stand out from routine status, e.g. the warning or error ink and kept on screen until the next action.\n\nSuggested labels: `bug`, `P2`, `area:ui`, `source:agent`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
